As is the case for fonts, the implementation for the registered colors must be available when the color is used in an image.  For Cedar users, the ColorRegistry provides these implementations.   All Cedar workstations and printers should have the ColorRegistry installed as a standard part of the environment (it only takes 1 GFI).  
